{"id":"s2","level":5,"levelName":"Structure and style","n":3,"of":10,"title":"If","titleHe":"תְּנַאי","goal":"Tell a real condition from an impossible one.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"אִם is for things that might happen, and takes the future. לוּ and אִילוּ are for things that didn't, and take the past — with הָיָה carrying the counterfactual."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"אִם יִהְיֶה זְמַן, נֵלֵךְ.","en":"If there's time, we'll go."},{"he":"אִילוּ יָדַעְתִּי, הָיִיתִי בָּא.","en":"Had I known, I would have come."},{"he":"לוּ הָיָה לִי כֶּסֶף…","en":"If only I had money…"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"The counterfactual is built with הָיָה plus the present participle: הָיִיתִי בָּא, I would have come. It's the one place the present tense is used to talk about the past."}],"vocab":[{"he":"אִם","en":"if","translit":"im"},{"he":"אִילוּ","en":"if (contrary to fact)","translit":"ilu"},{"he":"אוּלַי","en":"maybe","translit":"ulai"},{"he":"בְּלִי","en":"without","translit":"bli"},{"he":"אַף עַל פִּי כֵן","en":"nevertheless","translit":"af al pi chen"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["if","however, but","friend (f.)","solution"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אִם","translit":"im"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["conclusion","animal","then","if (contrary to fact)"],"correct":3,"prompt":"אִילוּ","translit":"ilu"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["lie, falsehood","pays","finds","maybe"],"correct":3,"prompt":"אוּלַי","translit":"ulai"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["cupboard, wardrobe","without","strength, power","lives, resides"],"correct":1,"prompt":"בְּלִי","translit":"bli"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["bicycle","with","friend (m.)","nevertheless"],"correct":3,"prompt":"אַף עַל פִּי כֵן","translit":"af al pi chen"},{"type":"choice","q":"“Had I known, I would have come.”","options":["אִילוּ יָדַעְתִּי, הָיִיתִי בָּא","אִם יָדַעְתִּי, אָבוֹא","אִם אֵדַע, בָּאתִי","אִילוּ אֵדַע, אֲנִי בָּא"],"correct":0,"why":"A condition that didn't happen takes אִילוּ with the past, and הָיָה plus the participle in the result."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “without”?","options":["אִם","אֵשׁ","חֵלֶק","בְּלִי"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"אוּלַי","translit":"ulai","en":"maybe"},{"type":"match","pairs":[["אִם","if"],["אִילוּ","if (contrary to fact)"],["אוּלַי","maybe"],["בְּלִי","without"],["אַף עַל פִּי כֵן","nevertheless"]]},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["בְּלִי","אִילוּ","אוּלַי","אִם"],"correct":1,"say":"אִילוּ","he":true},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"אִם ___ זְמַן, נֵלֵךְ.","en":"If there's time, we'll go.","options":["אִילוּ","יִהְיֶה","אוּלַי","אִם"],"correct":1,"full":"אִם יִהְיֶה זְמַן, נֵלֵךְ."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “if”?","options":["דִּבּוּר","אוּלַי","אִם","כַּעַס"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"לוּ הָיָה לִי ___","en":"If only I had money…","options":["אִילוּ","בְּלִי","כֶּסֶף…","אִם"],"correct":2,"full":"לוּ הָיָה לִי כֶּסֶף…"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “maybe”?","options":["מַסֶּכֶת","אוּלַי","דֹּאַר","נְיָר"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “nevertheless”?","options":["בִּכְלָל","נֶשֶׁר","מְנַסֶּה","אַף עַל פִּי כֵן"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “if (contrary to fact)” in Hebrew","answer":"אִילוּ","hint":"ilu"}]}